  "notes": "National Agricultural Development Co. (NADEC) — Saudi-Tadawul listed integrated dairy + agriculture group. Calendar fiscal year (Dec 31). Reportable IFRS 8 segments: Dairy + Foods (milk, juices, cheese, processed foods) and Agriculture (potato, vegetables, fruits, juice concentrate, olive oil — also includes large-scale arable farms in Saudi Arabia). NADEC owns ~50,000 ha (~124k acres) of farmland in Saudi Arabia (Haradh, Al-Jouf, Hail) including potato, alfalfa (legacy — winding down due to Saudi water restrictions on green-fodder cultivation), olives, table grapes. Most revenue (~75-80%) is dairy/foods; Agriculture is ~20-25%. Quarterly figures from Tadawul Form 8 quarterly disclosures and NADEC IR press releases; annual data from 2020-2024 annual reports. Net debt = total borrowings − cash & cash equivalents. Property book = property, plant & equipment + biological assets + bearer plants. Some segment splits estimated from disclosed annual breakdowns where quarterly disclosures are aggregate. Pre-2020 annual data (FY2000-FY2019) compiled from NADEC IR archive and Tadawul historical disclosures. NADEC was incorporated 1981 by Royal Decree as a Saudi government-backed agricultural co. Pre-2003 NADEC was primarily wheat + alfalfa + green fodder; dairy operations launched late 1990s and scaled materially in early-mid 2000s. Saudi Government's 2008-2018 phase-out of subsidised wheat (and 2015-2019 phase-out of subsidised green fodder/alfalfa) restructured the agriculture segment toward potato, olives, horticulture. Wafrah for Industry & Development merged into NADEC in 2020 (boosting share count from ~247m to ~290m). Earlier years had smaller acreage / agriculture-only profile; pre-2010 segment splits not consistently disclosed. Pre-2010 annual figures in nominal SAR millions per archived Saudi Capital Market Authority disclosures.",
